  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRCJR 2022-2023 (lead)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Joint Response Design for the period of 2022-2023 will be approached in the same way as the previous years: JR partners will collaborate at HZ levels, offering an integrated multi-sectoral response targeting the most vulnerable. The multi-sectoral approach is understood as an individual or community receiving a humanitarian assistance package of at least three sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Joint Response provides Food Security activities in all health zones. Education is promoted through WASH facilities in schools and snacks provided during catch-up classes. Child-Friendly Spaces will be created for play opportunities for children. This is for a multi-sectoral response.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The target group are the individuals affected by conflict. This includes, IDPs, returnees and host communities. In North Kivu the total number of beneficiaries directly benefiting from the joint response are 122.508, whilst in South Kivu this number is 118.586. Resulting in a total of 231.094 beneficiaries.</narrative>
  </description>
